---
// A rendered conversation, not a screenshot. The question is the one
// docs/demo.md tells a reader to ask first; the numbers are the measured
// Q2 answer in tests/fixtures/serving_questions.json, proven through the
// serving path by tests/test_serving_questions.py; the context lines quote
// what the fixture says the answer leans on. No product UI, no account.
import { DOC } from '../consts';
---

<div class="transcript" role="group" aria-label="A rendered example of the demo answering a cross-source question">
  <div class="msg user">
    <span class="who">you</span>
    <div class="body">
      <p>
        Using the metricmine-gold tools: do flights departing New York in an
        hour with precipitation at their origin run later than flights in a
        dry hour, and are they cancelled more often? Say what you joined on
        and what the context told you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="msg tools">
    <span class="who">tools</span>
    <div class="body">
      <ol class="calls">
        <li><code>list_fact_categories</code> <span>three categories, their typed marts, their registry keys</span></li>
        <li><code>get_context</code> <span>flights</span></li>
        <li><code>get_context</code> <span>airport_weather</span></li>
        <li><code>query</code> <span>one SELECT over the two typed marts</span></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="msg assistant">
    <span class="who">answer</span>
    <div class="body">
      <p>
        Yes on both counts. In hours with precipitation at the origin, flights
        left <strong>29.44 minutes</strong> late on average, and <strong>8.95 percent</strong> were
        cancelled (13,492 flights). In dry hours, <strong>12.42 minutes</strong> and <strong>2.41 percent</strong> (152,569
        flights).
      </p>
      <p>
        What I joined on: the conformed airport code and the conformed calendar
        hour, the cross-category join the registry declares. What the context
        told me: that join's measured completeness is 0.9994, so 97 flights fall
        outside it; and departure delay is null exactly when a flight is
        cancelled, so the averages exclude cancellations by construction and the
        cancellation rate comes from the flag.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <dl class="ledger">
    <div>
      <dt>data</dt>
      <dd>the two typed marts, joined as declared</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>expert context</dt>
      <dd>the declared join and its completeness; the null rule on departure delay</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
  <p class="foot">
    Rendered from the measured answer in{' '}
    <a href={DOC.questions}>serving_questions.json</a> (Q2), held by{' '}
    <a href={DOC.testServingQuestions}>test_serving_questions.py</a>. Not a
    screenshot.
  </p>
</div>

<style>
  .transcript {
    background: var(--mm-card-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--mm-border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 20px 22px 16px;
  }

  .msg {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 76px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 12px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--mm-border);
  }

  .msg:first-child {
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  .who {
    font-family: var(--font-jetbrains-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--mm-eyebrow);
    padding-top: 3px;
  }

  .body {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .msg p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .msg p + p {
    margin-top: 10px;
  }

  .msg.user p {
    color: var(--mm-text-2);
  }

  .msg strong {
    color: var(--mm-emph);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .calls {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-jetbrains-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .calls code {
    color: var(--mm-text);
    background: var(--mm-code-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--mm-border);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 0 5px;
  }

  .calls span {
    color: var(--mm-mono-sub);
  }

  .ledger {
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .ledger div {
    background: var(--mm-bg-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--mm-border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 10px 12px;
  }

  .ledger dt {
    font-family: var(--font-jetbrains-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--mm-eyebrow);
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }

  .ledger dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--mm-text-2);
  }

  .foot {
    margin: 14px 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-jetbrains-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--mm-mono-sub);
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .msg {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 4px;
    }

    .ledger {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
